Special Needs Today: by parents, for parents is a new one-stop shop web-based service which aims to provide timely and accurate information related to medical conditions and lifestyle issues experienced by children who have special needs.

The information is aimed at the following:

1. Parents and carers: helping them to better understand the challenges faced by their child by providing information written in plain English;

2. Medical professionals: saving time by enabling professionals involved in the care of special needs children to download information which can be passed to parents;

3. Schools: enabling staff within both mainstream academies and special schools to access and download information designed to help parents understand their child's care

Special Needs Today aims to assist a range of people involved in the care and welfare of children who have special needs.

The IDO (Intelligent Door Opener) is a clever tracking device that, when retrofitted to an existing automatic door, can significantly reduce false trigger rates.  It does this by monitoring the movement of people around the area of the door (both inside and outside the store) and only opens the door when someone walks towards the door rather than past it (or loiters around it).  

IDO has the following effects and benefits:
- Reduction in the amount of energy lost to the environment from heated or conditioned air leaving the building;
- In turn this reduces the load on the heating and cooling system to stabilise the temperature within the store and reduces the carbon footprint of the store;
- The building environment is more comfortable for both customers and staff thereby improving dwell time and staff churn;
- Door opening analysis allows any deviation from normal use to be spotted and reported centrally (e.g. doors locked open, etc).  

Independent tests by the Institute of Energy & Sustainable Development at De Montfort University have been used to estimate the potential energy savings by using the system.

Your Eastbourne BID is a business led, business funded organisation. It's purpose is to improve and enhance Eastbourne Town Centre.

Your Eastbourne BID will:

Enhance the environment with striking winter lighting, signage, and impactful planted areas whilst creating an identity to promote Eastbourne's independent shopping areas, like Little Chelsea, Terminus Road, Cornfield, Langney Road and Bolton Road;
Support and run events that will help increase footfall to our town;
Introduce family friendly street ambassadors at peak times to make our town safer;
Lobby all levels of Government to ensure the needs of our town centre are heard.

A one-stop-shop service for film and TV production-related activities in Hertfordshire.

Get in touch for support with:
- securing or offering film locations; 
- highway permits and liaising with regulatory bodies; 
- managing film applications; 
- and any general enquiries relating to film and TV production within Hertfordshire.

